  "result": "I've implemented `slugify` in `src/strings.js` and added 12 tests to `test/strings.test.js`. `npm test` passes all 14 tests, including the 2 that were already there.\n\n**How it works:**\n1. It splits each accented character into its base letter plus the accent mark, then removes the marks. That handles Vietnamese tones and other accents such as é and ñ, whether or not the input is already in split form.\n2. It lowercases the text.\n3. It replaces đ with d. Đ becomes đ when lowercased, so it ends up as d too. A few other Latin letters don't split off an accent this way, so I mapped them by hand: ø→o, ł→l, ß→ss, æ→ae, œ→oe, þ→th, ð→d, ħ→h and ı→i.\n4. It turns every run of characters other than a–z or 0–9 into a single hyphen, then trims hyphens from both ends.\n5. It cuts the result to 50 characters and removes any hyphen left at the end by the cut.\n\n**Tests cover:** basic lowercasing and hyphens, Vietnamese text, đ/Đ, other accented Latin text, input already in split form, collapsing runs of symbols, trimming, digits, input that ends up empty, the 50-character limit, a cut that lands on a hyphen, and a slug of exactly 50 characters.\n\nText in non-Latin scripts, such as Chinese or Cyrillic, has no letters left after these rules, so it becomes an empty string. That matches the rules as written.",
